{"kind":"assert","text":"H1 ruling on c439d8b6.\n\nItem 7, the reason codes. H1 adds no reason code. A code enters\n`REFUSAL_REASONS` and the class table in the head that first refuses\nwith it, with the property test for each `never` row. RC-1's rule\nneeds a judge site, and H1 has none. Remove the TODO from\n`packages/contract/src/read.ts`. The list lives in the note: H1 adds\none table to section 13.2 with each code, its class and the head that\nadds it.\n\nThe classes, as you propose, with two names changed:\n\n- `no-order`, never. It replaces `order-unavailable` as a refusal.\n  The note uses `order-unavailable` for two things: a scope with no\n  order, which is final, and an order scope that does not answer,\n  which passes. One name keeps one meaning. `order-unavailable` stays\n  an `UnavailableReason` only.\n- `not-a-member`, head. `order-forming`, head. `cut-gone` as the\n  refusal of an act, head.\n- `position-bound`, never. `not-open`, never. `allocation-expired`,\n  never.\n- `allocation-holed`, never. It replaces `holed` as a reason. `holed`\n  stays the name of the state.\n- `source-not-effective` takes the type and the place that\n  `source-unverified` has, and no class.\n- `member-pending` and `member-uncommitted` are `UnavailableReason`\n  only, and take no class.\n- `uncommitted` and `cut-gone` as answers of the `at` read stay in\n  `AtRead` only. They do not join `ReadRefusal`. H4 asks again if a\n  transport needs them.\n- `order-left` and `order-closed`: not in version 1.\n\nH1 corrects the note for the two names: sections 5.2, 5.3 and 5.4\nwhere they name the refusal, and the list of 13.2.\n\nChoices 1 to 5: confirmed. For choice 4, add one sentence to the H1\nnote: no service writes one of the six input kinds before H4, so\npromise 2 of the kernel page holds for every journal that a service\nwrites.\n\nThe open points:\n\na. `count` over a read. Keep the four forms that the validator\n   admits, and correct the list of section 5.2. Before H2 code, state\n   whether the example of section 7 and the absence rule of 5.7 need\n   `count` over a list, with a proposal.\nb. `part` on a read. Remove `part?` from the type of the `read`\n   operand. A member that the validator always refuses has no place\n   in the type. Say so first if a form of the corpus needs it.\nc. The range of a group read: `type` and `states` only. H5's package\n   check resolves the rest. Confirmed.\nd. The `page` byte domain: confirmed for H1. bytes refuses the kind\n   in records, so nothing reaches the throw. H4 names the domain.\ne. The `at` read over more than 64 items. No page is ever cut short,\n   because a short list gives `each` and `has` a wrong answer. The\n   read answers a refusal, and the reader's act is refused. H4\n   proposes the code and its class before code. Add the open point to\n   section 11 of the note.\n\nH1 then goes to its gate in the order of 02309bae, with LV1 after it.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}